  "result": "Perfect! I found the answer. The key requirement is **REQ-061** in the issues requirements document.\n\nREQ-061 states: \"Issue numbers are allocated per project and never reused\"\n\nThe critical detail is in the acceptance criteria and implementation description:\n- \"`nextIssueNumber(orgId, projectId)` returns a monotonically increasing integer **scoped to the project**\"\n- \"Numbers are never recycled\" **within their project scope**\n\nThis makes it perfectly correct for two different projects in the same workspace to each have issue #7, because issue numbers are scoped **per project**. A number is never handed out twice **within its own project scope**, which is exactly what the requirement specifies.\n\nANSWER: docs/requirements/issues.md",
